      "note": "`restored_relays` is how many relays this box re-energised from the last served restore. It is how the server learns the restore LANDED: a served restore followed by a zero \u2014 or by an absent field, which reads as zero \u2014 is the row an admin must see, because it means a court is dark that should not be. Omitted at zero, so a board with nothing to report sends the `heartbeat-request` body above, byte for byte.",
