    {
      "id": "heartbeat-request-relay-state",
      "note": "`relay_state` is what the box BELIEVES is closed, carried up from the Mega's !STATE, so the control board can say 'lights on \u2014 confirmed by the box' instead of only what it granted. Same pipe-delimited string array as the restore, for the same heapless-scanner reason, as <relay>|<remaining_seconds>. THREE STATES, NOT TWO: the key ABSENT means this firmware does not report relay state, an EMPTY ARRAY means the box believes nothing is closed. Both new fields must bind as nullable 64-bit on the server \u2014 an out-of-range value must not 400 the whole heartbeat, which is why no_push and events_lost are long? and not int?.",
