    {
      "id": "event-request-boot-id",
      "note": "The COURT BOX's event body carrying a real `boot_id` \u2014 the third field of the idempotency key (round G4, C2). The court box hardcodes 0 today, which omits the field; the server reads an absent boot_id as 0, which is exactly what (device, seq) always meant, so this vector is the change and not the status quo. Without it, a torn or erased seq checkpoint renumbers the board from 1 and every event of the next evening is receipted as a duplicate and discarded \u2014 including the `boot` event queued so an operator can see the board restarted. Position is part of the shape: immediately after `mac`, before `uptime_ms`.",
      "method": "POST",
